From 1d562c4f30cdbb16bf3586d112f28d2b5a9878cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] leds, regulator: add Samsung S2MPB02 flash LED and S2MPB02/03
 regulators

Camera PMICs of the Galaxy S10 family:

 - leds-s2mpb02: I2C driver for the flash LED channel of the S2MPB02.
   The torch is the LED class brightness (N x 20 mA, up to
   led-max-microamp), flash uses the LED flash class (N x 100 + 50 mA,
   hardware-timed timeout). As in the vendor driver the current is
   programmed over I2C and the TORCH/FLASH input pins switch the
   output; without the GPIOs the FLED_CTRL1 enable/mode bits are used.
 - s2mpb02-regulator: bucks, buck-boost and LDOs of the S2MPB02. The
   I2C client stays with the flash LED driver; this platform driver
   points at the chip with samsung,pmic and shares its regmap. Only
   regulators described in the DT are registered. Buck "disable"
   restores the reset value of the enable field, the state the
   bootloader leaves.
 - s2mpb03-regulator: I2C driver for the seven LDOs of the S2MPB03,
   with input supplies for the low-voltage and analog LDOs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
